          <h3>Charges and recurring billing</h3>
          <p>The checkout page displays the applicable one-time fee and subscription price. By completing checkout, you authorize the payment provider to charge your selected payment method for the amounts and schedule disclosed at checkout, including recurring monthly charges where applicable.</p>
          <h3>Automatic renewal</h3>
          <p>Subscriptions renew monthly until canceled, unless the checkout page or a written agreement states otherwise. The timing of your first subscription payment is the timing shown during checkout. Review that schedule before purchasing.</p>
          <h3>Cancellation</h3>
          <p>You may request cancellation using the method stated at checkout or by contacting us at [support email]. Unless applicable law requires otherwise or we agree in writing, cancellation takes effect at the end of the current paid billing period. You remain responsible for charges already incurred and services already provided.</p>
          <h3>Refunds</h3>
          <p>Any refund terms shown at checkout or in a written agreement apply. Unless otherwise stated in writing and subject to applicable law, website setup or project fees are generally nonrefundable once work begins, and subscription payments are generally not prorated after a billing period begins. Nothing here limits rights that cannot legally be waived.</p>
          <div class="policy-note"><p><strong>Before publishing:</strong> Confirm that billing timing, cancellation steps, and refund wording match your actual payment-provider settings and operations. Do not promise a cancellation method you have not implemented.</p></div>
        </section>
        <section class="policy-section" id="website-services">
          <h2>3. Website Projects, Hosting &amp; Support</h2>
          <h3>Project timing and revisions</h3>
          <p>Project timing begins after payment and receipt of required information and materials, unless otherwise agreed. Delays in receiving content, approvals, or feedback may extend delivery dates. Page counts, revisions, support tasks, and included features are determined by the selected offer or written agreement.</p>
          <h3>Hosting and maintenance</h3>
          <p>Hosting, maintenance, updates, and support are included only to the extent stated in your selected plan. Requests outside that scope may require an additional quote or fee. Maintenance may temporarily affect availability.</p>
          <h3>Ownership and transfer</h3>
          <p>Ownership of website content, source files, licenses, domains, accounts, and any right to transfer a website must be established in your written project agreement or offer. Third-party software, templates, stock assets, and platform features remain subject to their own license terms. Source files, licenses, and account transfers are not included unless expressly stated.</p>
          <h3>Customer-provided content</h3>
          <p>You are responsible for the accuracy, legality, and permissions associated with content and claims you provide, including testimonials, offers, images, and business information. You agree to review the final website and report errors promptly.</p>
          <h3>Suspension or termination</h3>
          <p>We may suspend or discontinue services for nonpayment, unlawful use, a material breach of these terms, or circumstances outside our reasonable control. Where practical, we will provide notice and an opportunity to address the issue. Post-cancellation access, export, or transfer assistance depends on the applicable plan and written agreement.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="policy-section" id="privacy">
          <h2>4. Privacy Policy</h2>
          <p>This section describes how Rebecca Bean Consulting may collect, use, and share personal information when you visit our website, contact us, purchase services, or complete a project form.</p>
          <h3>Information we collect</h3>
          <p>Depending on how you interact with us, information may include your name, business name, email address, phone number, billing or transaction details supplied by the payment processor, project information, messages, and technical information such as browser or website usage data.</p>
          <h3>How we use information</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>To respond to inquiries and provide purchased services.</li>
            <li>To process payments, manage subscriptions, and maintain business records.</li>
            <li>To send project updates, service notices, and support communications.</li>
            <li>To protect our website, prevent fraud, and meet legal obligations.</li>
            <li>To understand and improve our website and services where permitted.</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>How information is shared</h3>
          <p>We may share information with service providers needed to operate our business, such as website hosting, CRM, form, scheduling, email, payment, analytics, and automation providers. They may process information on our behalf under their own terms. We may also disclose information when required by law or to protect rights and safety. We do not sell personal information for money. If our actual use of advertising or analytics technologies constitutes a “sale,” “sharing,” or targeted advertising under applicable law, we will provide required notices and choices.</p>
          <h3>Retention and security</h3>
          <p>We retain information for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described above, including business, tax, legal, dispute-resolution, and recordkeeping needs. We use reasonable safeguards, but no online transmission or storage system can be guaranteed completely secure.</p>
          <h3>Your privacy choices</h3>
          <p>Depending on your location and applicable law, you may have rights to request access to, correction of, or deletion of personal information, or to opt out of certain uses. Contact us using the details below. We may need to verify your identity before responding.</p>
          <h3>Children</h3>
          <p>Our website and services are intended for businesses and adults, not children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information online from children under 13.</p>
          <h3>Changes to this policy</h3>
          <p>We may update this policy as our services or legal requirements change. We will post the updated version here and revise the “Last updated” date.</p>
        </section>
